!! Article reader

The article reader gives DOI-backed literature tiddlers a cleaner reading surface than raw publisher HTML.

!! Workflow

# Save publisher HTML for a paper, typically with SingleFile, and upload it through the `/literature/upload-html` route.
# The plugin extracts the DOI from the HTML and matches it to an existing `bibtex-entry` tiddler.
# Open the saved article at `/literature/article/<title>`.

PubConnector and SingleFile work well together for this capture flow: SingleFile preserves the publisher page, and PubConnector can stay in the loop for the related browser-side workflow.

!! Reader features

* Text highlighting with five reading categories.
* Optional notes on each highlight.
* Highlight notes rendered as wikitext when displayed.
* Highlight note review through the `highlight-notes` widget.
* Font size controls for long reading sessions.
* Domain auto-linking that turns concept names into links back to the wiki.

!! Domain auto-linking

The article route can inject a gradual domain-linking pass so article rendering stays responsive.

Open [[$:/plugins/bangyou/tw-pubconnector/settings/article]] to configure:

* whether domain auto-linking is enabled
* the filter that chooses candidate concept tiddlers
* the ignore field used to blacklist selected concepts
* the alias field used for alternate terms
* whether only the first occurrence per paragraph should be linked

This is useful for building concept-rich reading views without manually editing article HTML.